    "narrative": "For today's matchup, the Austin Waves lineup is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (73.73) and **Andy Pages** (68.03). Both outfielders draw favorable matchups against Gallen, benefiting from neutral platoon splits and advantageous lineup positioning. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, with his 73.73 score driven by a strong base projection and a subtle boost from hitting in the 5-hole. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.40) also projects as a high-floor cornerstone today, overcoming a dynamic platoon disadvantage against Holmes to remain a locked-in start due to his superior xwOBA metrics. We are looking for these three to drive our counting stats, as the remaining roster relies heavily on favorable park factors to counteract mediocre SP matchups.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Miguel Vargas**, who landed just shy of our starters with a 51.38 score. While his placement in the #2 hole provided a significant boost, he was ultimately benched in favor of **Coby Mayo** (52.06) and **Sam Antonacci** (54.78), both of whom offered marginally higher efficiency in the daily model. Notably, **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio** were considered for their potential stolen base upside\u2014a critical category for our 5x5 Roto standing\u2014but their bottom-of-the-order assignments pushed their efficiency scores below our optimal threshold. We continue to monitor **Jackson Merrill**, whose 38.94 score reflects the heavy penalty of facing a tough southpaw like S\u00e1nchez; he remains on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable platoon matchups.\n\nRisk mitigation is the theme of the day, particularly regarding our middle infielders. **Gunnar Henderson** (53.96) is facing Tolle, and while the park factor is favorable, the combination of a left-on-left disadvantage and an elite opposing SP creates a lower-than-usual ceiling. We are keeping a close watch on the weather and official lineups, as any late-breaking shifts\u2014especially for **Sam Antonacci** at the lead-off spot\u2014could necessitate a pivot. Despite the lack of an elite blowout spot, the lineup is optimized to maximize plate appearances while keeping our 5x5 categories competitive, prioritizing high-contact, high-OBP profiles to navigate today\u2019s difficult slate of opposing arms.",
